<p>Nepal votes on March 5 in snap parliamentary elections to fill all 275 seats in the House of Representatives—the country’s first national vote since youth-led protests against corruption brought down the previous government and sped up the election timetable. The campaign has been shaped by high expectations—especially among younger voters—for visible reforms, cleaner governance, and more opportunity, with many activists urging voters to replace long-established political figures with new leadership. But the vote also comes with unresolved tensions from last year’s unrest, sharpening calls for accountability—and for a peaceful, credible election. Alongside the generational push for change, observers point to persistent representation gaps: one report says women make up about 10% of the more than 3,400 candidates contesting seats in the direct vote, raising fresh questions about how inclusive post-uprising politics will be.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DsVoAey7q-ooDb8eWzVBquOOivR8_pxQjw2dXA2tBy_IbbrIIYa-g8tCXVTpgnJh7DxIgzN5ZhzDtKNqee5_9cLWE1lUR2lkFaheS1-Vxt1Nuz1-ihxHDgK6LX3fc-3MB168T9bW2DyZspLtAdUwn6CqlCbUYxOzbEeBQewUQNLAQWhRN0tMeq5Roeiu0c0ZZqOXg2sb' alt='People attend a campaign rally in Kathmandu ahead of Nepal’s March 5 vote.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>How voting works: Voters choose 165 lawmakers directly, and parties fill 110 seats through proportional representation—a mixed system meant to balance local races with overall party strength.</li><li>Scale of the electorate: Nearly 19 million people can vote in a country of about 30 million, according to election reporting ahead of polling day.</li><li>Campaign dynamics: Analysts say anti-incumbency—and a potentially decisive youth vote—could lift newer forces such as the Rastriya Swatantra Party. Kathmandu mayor Balendra Shah, 35, is often cited as a popular figure who reflects the pull of younger leadership.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Gen Z activists and young voters: Youth organizers and voters have pressed for political reform and “new faces,” arguing that corruption, nepotism, and limited opportunities have held their generation back. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-elections-gen-z-hopes-for-genuine-political-reforms/a-76200486'>DW</a>)</li><li>Election administrators (process focus): Reporting on the election rules emphasizes a mixed electoral system—direct seats plus proportional representation—and explains how ballots are counted, framing legitimacy around transparent procedures. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepal-election-2026-explained-how-voting-and-counting-work-11128538#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Women candidates and advocates: A report highlighting candidate lists says women account for only about 10% of the more than 3,400 candidates in the direct races, pointing to continued barriers to political participation even after the uprising. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepal-elections-2026-nepali-women-sidelined-in-post-uprising-polls-11166100#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Political establishment figures: Veteran leaders remain on the ballot—including former prime minister Madhav Kumar Nepal, who filed to contest from the Rautahat 1 constituency—while some coverage describes a tougher environment for long-dominant figures like K. P. Sharma Oli and Pushpa Kamal Dahal ‘Prachanda’ amid shifting voter expectations. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepals-march-5-vote-waves-coalitions-and-the-new-guard-on-the-cards/article70699719.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-elections-gen-z-hopes-for-genuine-political-reforms/a-76200486'>Nepal elections: Gen Z hopes for genuine political reforms</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepal-election-2026-madhav-kumar-nepal-from-cpnuml-veteran-to-unified-socialist-11138163#publisher=newsstand'>Nepal Election 2026: Madhav Kumar Nepal: From CPNUML Veteran To Unified Socialist</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/04/world/asia/nepal-election-gen-z-what-to-know.html'>What to Know About Nepal&#x27;s Gen Z Election</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-03/nepals-generation-z-seeks-to-defeat-the-old-guard-in-the-upcoming-elections-we-want-to-see-new-faces.html'>Nepal’s Generation Z seeks to defeat the old guard in the upcoming elections: ‘We want to see new faces’</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-2026-gen-z-demands-political-change/article70702043.ece'>Nepal’s general election on March 5 seeks political change</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>